<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Uganda Protectorate</h1><p class="st-meta">1894 CE – 1962 CE · capital Entebbe</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British protectorate built around the Kingdom of Buganda, which kept African kingdoms and farmers at its heart and became independent Uganda in 1962.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imperial-british-east-africa-company">Imperial British East Africa Company</a> withdrew, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Buganda</a> in 1894 and extended it to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro">Bunyoro</a>, Toro, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Ankole</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/busoga-principalities">Busoga</a> in the following years, after defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabalega">Kabalega</a> of Bunyoro. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buganda-agreement">Buganda Agreement</a> of 1900, negotiated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harry-johnston">Harry Johnston</a>, set the terms of British rule and Buganda's privileged place.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ruled indirectly, using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baganda">Ganda</a> chiefs as agents across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and preserving the kingdoms. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uganda-railway">Uganda Railway</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a> in 1901, and African smallholders grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>, with Indian traders handling much of the commerce. Christian missions spread rapidly. The exile of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutesa-ii-of-buganda">Kabaka Mutesa II</a> from 1953 to 1955 sparked a major crisis.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/uganda">Uganda</a> became independent on 9 October 1962 under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a>, with the kingdoms federated within it, and in 1963 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutesa-ii-of-buganda">Mutesa II</a> became president. Tensions between the central state and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Buganda</a> shaped its early politics.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/uganda-protectorate.jpg" alt="Uganda Protectorate" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Uganda_Protectorate.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1894 CE – 1962 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Entebbe</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Harry Johnston, Andrew Cohen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, traditional religion, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Luganda, Swahili</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uganda">Uganda</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Uganda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=uganda-protectorate" aria-label="Uganda Protectorate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5582 2176 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Uganda Protectorate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5902 2432L5865 2378M5902 2432L5900 2421M5902 2432L5841 2409M5902 2432L5852 2457M5902 2432L5923 2416M5902 2432L4997 651M5902 2432L6101 2585M5902 2432L5905 2422"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5865 2378h0M5900 2421h0M5841 2409h0M5852 2457h0M5923 2416h0M4997 651h0M6101 2585h0M5905 2422h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d=